WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.720
- I worry, genuinely,
about the consequences

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.280
of a doctor who has a large following

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.090
telling his audience to use something

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.680
that he knows is not safe
and carries serious risk.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.430
Hey, guys, welcome to another episode

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.700
of the Wednesday Checkup.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.950
I've been finding myself spending

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.530
a lot of time on Twitter lately,

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.540
trying to get the most
up-to-date information

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.390
about coronavirus out there,

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:20.900
as well as leaning at the same time,

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.650
and I've come across a few doctors

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.490
that have found themselves in hot water

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.090
after making some
statements about COVID-19.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.040
Before we start, I wanna give
a huge thank you once again

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:31.820
to the healthcare frontline workers.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.560
Doctors, pharmacists, nurses,

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.150
everyone that's helping battle COVID-19.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.927
Seriously, from the bottom
of my heart, thank you.

00:00:38.927 --> 00:00:41.510
(techno music)

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:43.663
(static buzzing)

00:00:43.663 --> 00:00:45.840
Let's start off with Dr. Drew

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.430
who seems to be in the
most hot water right now.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:50.770
Mostly about his statements
that he made prior

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:53.010
to the coronavirus becoming a pandemic.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.860
- Way less virulant than the flu.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:55.720
That should be the headline,

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.210
way less serious than influenza.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.480
Should the Olympics be canceled?

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.313
That's funny.

00:00:59.313 --> 00:01:00.800
DeBlasio told them not to ride the trains,

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:02.230
so they're not riding the trains,

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:04.070
and so I am (laughing).

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:05.470
I mean, it's ridiculous.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:09.640
The flu virus in this country
is vastly more consequential.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.720
It is a press induced panic.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.850
- Twitter absolutely exploded
once this video went live

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.470
and got millions of views
seemingly in minutes.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:20.160
And look, I'm not gonna lie,
I got emotional watching this.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:21.240
I got riled up.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.640
I tell people to not get anxious

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.950
because once they get emotional
they make bad decisions,

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.410
and here I was getting upset.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.820
The reason why I got
emotional in watching that

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.120
is because I started thinking about

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.880
the potential consequences
that could come about

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.350
when a trusted figure like Dr. Drew

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.160
tells people to now worry
about this novel coronavirus.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.020
Did they go out?

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:40.490
Were they exposed to this virus?

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:41.980
Did they get potentially really sick

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:43.170
and even lose their lives?

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:46.210
Where I think Dr. Drew
took his biggest misstep

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.610
was not the fact that he was wrong about

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.710
the novel coronavirus, we're all entitled

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.630
to be wrong as experts, as doctors,

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.060
because medicine is an imperfect science.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.800
I've said in other videos how medicine

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.810
is as much art as it is science

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.080
because two doctors can
look the same situation

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.870
and have different interpretations of it.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:06.000
I think where he went wrong
was he forgot, somewhat,

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.250
that medicine carries within
itself a level of humility,

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.250
we have to approach it
with a level of humility.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.737
To me, if Dr. Drew came out
and said something like,

00:02:13.737 --> 00:02:15.867
"Look, I think in my own expert opinion

00:02:15.867 --> 00:02:17.837
"that this novel
coronavirus won't be as bad

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.537
"as the media is making it seem,

00:02:19.537 --> 00:02:21.570
"but we'll keep looking
at the information,"

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.630
I think that would have been a
reasonable statement to make,

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:25.250
even though he was wrong at the end.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:28.650
All of this really serves
as a stark reminder

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.700
that expert opinion is
and should always be

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.000
considered the lowest form of evidence.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.770
When we talk about levels of evidence,

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:37.120
we look at expert opinion,

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:39.140
basically what a doctor thinks is right,

00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.710
then we move on to a case
series, observational studies,

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:45.510
then the gold standard
randomized controlled studies.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.410
And you even have one up on that,

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:49.050
where you have a meta analyses,

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.610
which is many randomized
controlled studies.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.370
I am pleased to report, though,

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.120
that Dr. Drew did issue this apology.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.740
- My early comments about equating

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:02.830
coronavirus with influenza, were wrong.

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:04.060
They were incorrect.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.247
I was part of a course
that was saying that,

00:03:06.247 --> 00:03:07.720
and we were wrong.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.790
And I want to apologize for that.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.020
- Interestingly, the verb
that we use for medicine

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.340
is practicing, we practice medicine,

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.970
because we're all bound to make a mistake,

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:18.650
especially with how
imperfect our knowledge is,

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.370
we're continuously evolving
it and doing better,

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.420
and trying harder.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.090
All in all, I hope to see Dr. Drew

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.710
bounce back from this incident.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.170
I know millions of people look

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:29.300
to Dr. Drew for medical advice,

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.170
and he brings a really
unique vantage point

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:33.830
to medical media, being that
he's duly board certified

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:36.350
in addiction and internal medicine,

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:38.047
with a huge focus on mental health.

00:03:38.047 --> 00:03:38.880
(record scratching)

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.520
I've heard that Dr Drew's media team

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.020
has been issuing copyright
take-down notices

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.250
for people using the
clips that I just used,

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.590
I really hope they don't come after us

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:48.310
as this is a good learning opportunity.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:50.550
Next up, we have another popular

00:03:50.550 --> 00:03:52.740
medical media figure: Dr. Oz.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:55.010
He received some serious
backlash on Twitter

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:57.380
for comments he made on
Fox News, take a look.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:58.960
The panic attack is devastating

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:00.730
and it is a physical problem.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:03.070
It's not just in your
head, your whole body,

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.430
the rapid palpitations, the sweating,

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:08.250
the feeling that the world
is closing in around you,

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:09.950
and these symptoms can cause all kinds

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.700
of detrimental effects, which is why

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:13.480
I think a lot of doctors now are feeling

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:15.800
that the worry and the
panic about coronavirus

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.930
is gonna be worse than the
actual coronavirus for them.

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:20.320
- The majority of criticism from Twitter

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.860
came from the fact that they felt Dr. Oz

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:26.670
was misrepresenting the views
of doctors on the front lines,

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:30.130
who are legitimately more
concerned about coronavirus

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:32.300
than they anxiety that can
potentially come from it.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.840
I actually happen to agree
with Twitter on this one.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.120
I have a lot of Doctor friends
who are on the frontlines.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.480
A great example would
be Dr. Donald Pettit,

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.910
who was actually in my
hundred doctors video,

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:45.050
he's an ER resident who happens

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.970
to be working in the ICU right now,

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.290
he tells me about the equipment shortages,

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.830
the ICU and ventilator use that's gone up

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:55.530
tremendously over the last few
weeks, and it's scary to him.

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:57.370
I mean he's on the front lines potentially

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:00.550
getting himself sick, bringing
the virus home to his family.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:02.300
He has a newborn baby at home,

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.410
so I actually went
ahead and texted Dr. Oz.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.620
I mentioned the negative
criticism he was getting,

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:09.250
my thoughts on the subject,
and I'm happy to report

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:10.910
he was quite welcoming of that,

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.110
and he said that in the
following interviews

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:14.700
he was going to make a change in the way

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.440
he spoke about this, and
correct his previous statements.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.030
I do live television quite often,

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:23.880
and I know how easy it is to
have one thing in your mind,

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:26.540
and then speak something that
comes out somewhat different.

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:28.510
So I was appreciating the fact that Dr. Oz

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.220
was open to this type of feedback,

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.700
and was willing to change
his statements in the future.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.560
I think that's how we as
doctors really have to function

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.060
in order to be more
effective communicators

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:40.910
and better at relaying
crucial medical information

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:42.040
to the general public.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:44.730
Up next, we have quite a polarizing figure

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:46.640
in Dr. Joseph Mercola.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:49.280
Dr. Joseph Mercola is
a practicing physician,

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:51.280
he takes a naturopathic approach

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:54.450
to how he treats his patients,
he's quite popular online.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:56.580
He's actually found
himself in hot water quite

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.000
a few times with the FDA for making

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.910
unsubstantiated claims about products

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:02.170
that he sells on his website,

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.810
and I haven't really found any claims

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:07.300
that I was interested
in debunking until I saw

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.600
a few recent tweets that
caught my attention.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.217
The first tweet reads as such,

00:06:11.217 --> 00:06:13.867
"While unproven, one
current theory is that

00:06:13.867 --> 00:06:15.727
"electromagnetic field radiation,

00:06:15.727 --> 00:06:17.797
"and the addition of 5G in particular,

00:06:17.797 --> 00:06:20.830
"could be having an impact
on the COVID-19 pandemic."

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:23.220
This is actually a very
common conspiracy theory

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:26.070
that's being put out there
on social media forums,

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.410
on Reddit, what have you.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:29.320
Here's the problem, no evidence exists

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:30.620
to support this theory.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:34.230
Let me talk about briefly how
we create theories in science

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:35.630
and then how we go about testing them.

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:39.240
First and foremost, you
have to have an idea

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:43.110
with a plausible mechanism
of how that idea comes to be.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:45.700
For example, if you wanted
to create antibiotics

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.110
before there were antibiotics,

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:48.247
you had to think to yourself,

00:06:48.247 --> 00:06:50.987
"Well, this antibiotic
can work in this method

00:06:50.987 --> 00:06:52.427
"to kill this bacteria,

00:06:52.427 --> 00:06:54.570
"thereby eliminating it from the system."

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.320
You go ahead, you try it in lab models,

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:58.510
animal models, human models,
and you work your way up.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:01.690
Here, there is no plausible mechanism

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:05.490
for how EMF waves or 5G makes people have

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.410
worse cases of the novel coronavirus.

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.820
That's why I wish this tweet ended

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:11.390
when he said, "While unproven."

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:12.900
Because while it's unproven,

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:15.370
we can make any random
correlative statement.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:18.740
The fact that February
had an extra day this year

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:22.410
could be a reason why COVID-19
is affecting us so seriously.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:24.510
You can really substitute
that with anything,

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:26.660
and that goes to speak to the power

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:29.480
of the difference between
correlation and causation.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:32.520
Remember, correlation, two
things happening simultaneously,

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.000
5G and coronavirus.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:36.240
Causation is when something directly

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:37.680
causes that thing to happen.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:38.930
The next tweet, which I think

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:41.557
is the more problematic
of the two, reads of such.

00:07:41.557 --> 00:07:43.597
"Nebulized hydrogen peroxide therapy

00:07:43.597 --> 00:07:45.337
"is an inexpensive and simple way

00:07:45.337 --> 00:07:48.177
"to treat most viral
respiratory illnesses,

00:07:48.177 --> 00:07:50.437
"all you need is a
nebulizer with a face mask

00:07:50.437 --> 00:07:51.837
"that covers your mouth and nose,

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:53.987
"and common household hydrogen peroxide

00:07:53.987 --> 00:07:56.690
"available at most grocery
stores and pharmacies."

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:58.160
Now, there's a few things to unpack here.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:02.240
First and foremost, the
CDC and FDA clearly state

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:04.620
that there exists no proven methods

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:07.090
to treat or prevent COVID-19.

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:10.730
And to me, when a doctor
believes their own expert opinion

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:13.820
outweighs those of major
medical organizations,

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:17.020
like the CDC and FDA,
without substantial evidence,

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:18.000
you're crossing a line.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.230
Next, let's talk about the dangers

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:22.460
of inhaled hydrogen peroxide.

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:23.857
Straight from the CDC website,

00:08:23.857 --> 00:08:26.757
"Hydrogen peroxide is
not absorbed by the skin,

00:08:26.757 --> 00:08:30.830
"but can cause systemic toxicity
when inhaled or ingested."

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:32.320
I have to read this next whole segment

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.457
because of how serious it is.

00:08:33.457 --> 00:08:36.357
"Vapors, mist, or aerosols
of hydrogen peroxide

00:08:36.357 --> 00:08:38.507
"can cause upper airway irritation,

00:08:38.507 --> 00:08:41.477
"inflammation of the nose,
hoarseness, shortness of breath,

00:08:41.477 --> 00:08:44.017
"and a sensation of burning
or tightness in the chest.

00:08:44.017 --> 00:08:46.237
"Exposure to high
concentrations can result

00:08:46.237 --> 00:08:49.747
"in severe mucosal congestion
of the trachea and bronchitis

00:08:49.747 --> 00:08:52.337
"and delayed accumulation
of fluid in the lungs."

00:08:52.337 --> 00:08:54.917
"Children may be more
vulnerable to corrosive agents

00:08:54.917 --> 00:08:56.647
"than adults because of the relatively

00:08:56.647 --> 00:08:58.800
"smaller diameter of their airways."

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:02.320
Dr. Mercola, in his own YouTube video,

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:05.160
actually states that you should not use

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:07.420
common household hydrogen peroxide.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:09.720
- The companies put in stabilizers there,

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:11.710
and they're pretty much all proprietary,

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:13.140
so they don't have to disclose

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:15.320
what those specific stabilizers are,

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:16.870
but believe me they are not intended

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:18.190
for human use or consumption,

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:21.280
and they are not cleared
for safety studies

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:22.120
for human consumption.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.080
So these are not designed to be typically

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.748
swallowed, ingested, or inhaled.

00:09:26.748 --> 00:09:30.740
- I worry genuinely about the consequences

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:32.932
of a doctor who has a large following

00:09:32.932 --> 00:09:35.240
telling his audience to use something that

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.750
he knows is not safe and
carries serious risk.

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:40.440
Do not nebulize hydrogen peroxide,

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:42.810
do not think it's gonna
eliminate COVID-19,

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:44.900
it's not proven, it's not smart,

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:46.600
and it's potentially very dangerous.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.390
I actually reached out
to a Board Certified

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:51.430
pediatric ICU physician,
Dr. David Epstein,

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:53.670
you may have seen him on
my hundred doctors video,

00:09:53.670 --> 00:09:55.577
and he said quote, unquote,

00:09:55.577 --> 00:09:57.947
"So shameful to take
advantage of people like this

00:09:57.947 --> 00:09:59.307
"and potentially cause harm.

00:09:59.307 --> 00:10:00.997
"I've never heard of anyone doing this

00:10:00.997 --> 00:10:03.087
"and can help to think that someone

00:10:03.087 --> 00:10:05.437
"won't walk away with
some kind of pneumonitis.

00:10:05.437 --> 00:10:07.847
"I just hope they don't
listen to this advice.

00:10:07.847 --> 00:10:09.600
"Totally unethical."

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:10.720
I 100% agree.

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:13.450
I really hope Dr. Mercola
issues a retraction

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:16.350
and tells his audience, which
is a rather large audience,

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:19.150
the danger of doing this
with hydrogen peroxide.

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:22.290
Please click here for my
hundred doctors video,

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:25.410
I literally interviewed
100 doctors in seven days.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:27.570
Yes this entire video
was made in seven days.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:30.600
These doctors took out the time
to get you the information,

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.490
